----------------------------------------------------------------------
3. structure_graph FLOW (mirrors analyze_mesh error-envelope ordering)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. _cm_to_unit_factor(units) -> ValueError => {"error": <msg>}
2. raw = _call("extract_mesh_data", {"mesh": mesh})
3. Envelopes, in analyze_mesh's exact order:
     raw.startswith("Error: ")            -> {"error": rest}
     raw.startswith(("Cannot reach",
                     "Unexpected error")) -> return raw verbatim
     json.loads(raw) ValueError          -> return raw verbatim
     "error" in data                     -> {"error": data["error"]}
4. decompose_result = mesh_analysis.decompose_mesh_faces(nodes, indices)
5. graph = mesh_graph.build_structure_graph(decompose_result)
6. Algorithms:
     articulation_points = sorted(nx.articulation_points(graph))
     components = list(nx.connected_components(graph))
     graph.graph["articulation_points"] = articulation_points
     graph.graph["connected_components"] = [sorted(c) for c in components]
     Face nodes in articulation_points -> is_articulation_point = True
     (set BEFORE _persist_to_duckdb so the flag lands as a nodes column)
7. conn = mesh_graph._persist_to_duckdb(graph, mesh)   # key = mesh param
8. Summary computed AFTER persist so duckdb_table_schema reflects reality.
9. json.dumps(summary, indent=2)
10. Steps 4-8 wrapped: except Exception -> {"error": "structure graph failed: ..."}

